- **Document core (blitz-dom):** `Document` trait — `inner`, `inner_mut`, default `handle_ui_event` via `EventDriver` with `NoopEventHandler`, default `poll` returning `false`, `id`, and — under the `accessibility` feature — a default `accessibility_tree() -> accesskit::TreeUpdate` returning `self.inner().build_accessibility_tree()`, which a wrapper may override to enrich nodes (`DioxusDocument` alone does, with stable ids) (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:165-199), implemented for `PlainDocument`, `BaseDocument`, `Rc<RefCell<BaseDocument>>` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:201-228), `HtmlDocument` (packages/blitz-html/src/html_document.rs:7-70), `ScriptDocument` (packages/blitz-vibey-script/src/document.rs:393-437) and `DioxusDocument` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:239-311); `DocGuard`/`DocGuardMut` wrap a borrowed `BaseDocument` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:113-163); `DocumentConfig` fields: viewport, base_url, ua_stylesheets, net/navigation/shell/html-parser providers, font_ctx, media_type, style_threading, incremental, abort_signal, subdocument_depth, clock (packages/blitz-dom/src/config.rs:29-72) — `ua_stylesheets` a `Vec<UserAgentStylesheet>` since 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship (was `Option<Vec<String>>`), a hand-written `Default` setting it to the one default sheet, `UserAgentStylesheet::default_sheet()`, a `LazyLock` parse of `DEFAULT_CSS`, and a config that sets it used as given (packages/blitz-dom/src/config.rs:35-39; packages/blitz-dom/src/config.rs:74-93; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:82); `DocumentEvent` messages `ResourceLoad(ResourceLoadResponse)` and `NavigateIframe { node_id, url }` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:230-238);
 `Resource` enum Image, Svg, Css, ImportedCss, Font, DocumentSrc, None and `ResourceLoadResponse { request_id, node_id, resolved_url, Result<Resource, String> }` (packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:57-69; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:128-134); `NetHandler::bytes(resolved_url, bytes)` per resource kind (packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:143-176; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:547-552; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:563-568); the changed set — `BaseDocument::has_changes(&self) -> bool` reads true while the changed set (`changed_nodes`, a `pub(crate)` `HashSet<NodeId>`) is non-empty, from the first tracked write until the next drain, and `BaseDocument::take_changed_nodes(&mut self) -> HashSet<NodeId>` returns the set and leaves it empty; a returned id may name a node dropped since it was written, so it is read through `get_node`, never by indexing; node creation marks nothing — `create_node` no longer inserts, so the constructor's root node, the mutator's `create_element` / `create_text_node` and layout's anonymous blocks and pseudo-element nodes leave the set empty; what does mark it is stated under §Cross-cutting Patterns → Invalidation and state integrity; `has_changes` has no caller outside tests — the windowed shell drains instead (the next contract); before 2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff `has_changes` returned `changed_nodes.is_empty()` over a set the constructor filled through `create_node` and nothing drained, and read false after an in-document write (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/evidence/control-changed-set.txt); ratified by the founder (2026-10-07) — the engine half of one item with the shell's refresh on change, which changes behaviour for every Blitz document (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:366-369; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:955-961; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1119-1132)
 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot two public read-only methods: `BaseDocument::can_paint_text(&self) -> bool` — whether the font context resolves a family for the `sans-serif` generic, through fontique's `generic_families` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1134-1147) — and `BaseDocument::layout_as_text_input(&self, node_id, text) -> Option<parley::Layout<TextBrush>>` — `text` laid out with a text input's editor styles, scale and direction in the document's own fonts, one unbroken line, a fresh `LayoutContext` per call, `None` for a node that is no text input; its two callers are blitz-paint's password mask, which holds no font context of its own, and blitz-dom's password click caret (`click_password_input`, packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:582-648) (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1149-1179); public re-exports from the crate root (packages/blitz-dom/src/lib.rs:77-132)

- **Mutation, query and CSSOM:** `doc.mutate()` methods `create_element`, `create_text_node`, `set_attribute`, `clear_attribute`, `append_children`, `insert_nodes_before`, `remove_node`, `remove_and_drop_node`, `set_inner_html`, `set_node_text`, `set_custom_widget`, `set_style_property` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/detached_attribute.rs:27-36; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:484-494; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:517-528; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:554; tests/blitz-tests/tests/incremental_oracle.rs:588; tests/blitz-tests/tests/custom_widget_layout.rs:40; tests/blitz-tests/tests/line_break.rs:46-49; tests/blitz-tests/tests/animations.rs:23); selector API `query_selector`, `query_selector_all`, `query_selector_in`, `query_selector_all_in`, `matches_selector`, `closest`, `try_parse_selector_list` and node-level raw variants, returning `Result` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scoped_query_selector.rs:46-66; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scoped_query_selector.rs:158-174), as `Result<Option<NodeId>, ParseError>` / `Result<SmallVec<[NodeId; 32]>, ParseError>` never matching the scope node (packages/blitz-dom/src/query_selector.rs:57-83; packages/blitz-dom/src/query_selector.rs:117-141); CSSOM addresses stylesheets by owner `NodeId` and rules by an index path (packages/blitz-dom/src/cssom.rs:4-8) with `CssRuleInfo` snapshots (packages/blitz-dom/src/cssom.rs:82-97); `resolved_style_value` returns an empty string for unknown properties and used values for layout-dependent ones (packages/blitz-dom/src/resolved_style.rs:336-343); `RequestContentType` urlencoded, multipart, text/plain (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:398-429); `BoundingRect { x, y, width, height }` in f64 (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3097-3103); `build_accessibility_tree` returns an accesskit `TreeUpdate` of `(NodeId, accesskit::Node)` pairs, naming a node from five sources
 — its direct text children (`labelled_by` its `TextRun`s), an `aria-label` non-empty after trimming (`label`, accname-1.2 §2C), a `<label>` bound through `label_bound_input_element` (its `for`-target labelable element by id, else its first nested labelable element — HTML's labelable elements, `button`, an `input` whose `type` is not `hidden` (ASCII case-insensitive), `meter`, `output`, `progress`, `select` and `textarea`, matched by the private `is_labelable`), pushed onto the bound element's `labelled_by` after the visit when both have built nodes, a select's option's non-empty `label` attribute where it has no `aria-label` (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:36-61; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:151-163; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:677-715; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3126-3140), and, since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync (upstream's reads as upstream wrote them, merged at `23b9b26a9`), `aria-labelledby`: after the `<label>` → input loop it clears the node's `labelled_by`, pushes the referenced nodes that have built nodes (an id naming no element ignored, `referenced_dom_ids_to_node_ids`) and sets their text, gathered through `write_text_alternative` · `write_flat_text_content` · `FlatText`, as the computed `label` (`set_label`), so it outranks a `<label>` and an `aria-label` (accname 2B over 2C/2D), the `aria-label` the fallback when the targets hold no text (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:62-103; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:119-126; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:276-327; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_label.rs:30-297);
 the same sync's builder also reads `aria-describedby` (the referenced built nodes pushed as `described_by`), `aria-description` (its own text into AccessKit's description field), `aria-expanded` (a boolean), `aria-disabled` (`true` sets AccessKit disabled) and `aria-level` (a number, with defaults by tag and role, `default_level_for_tag` · `default_level_for_role`), then `set_html_tag` last (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:214-241; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:417-438; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_description.rs:8-93); our trimmed non-empty `aria-label` read and the closed-set `aria-selected` · `aria-pressed` · `aria-invalid` reads below are kept, and upstream's own `aria-selected` (`parse::<bool>`) and unfiltered `aria-label` reads were dropped in the merge, so the builder reads each attribute once; since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states the builder (`BaseDocument::build_accessibility_node`, private) also reads state attributes on every element — a select's option excepted, whose `selected` is its chosen state, true or false, with no `aria-selected` read (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:171-181) —, the toggle by role, each value trimmed of ASCII whitespace and compared exactly, in lower case — `aria-selected`: `true` / `false` sets AccessKit `selected` true / false, anything else nothing; `aria-pressed`: `true` · `false` · `mixed` sets `toggled` `True` · `False` · `Mixed`, anything else nothing, on every role but the five checkable ones; `aria-checked`: the same three values set `toggled` on a role in the private `is_checkable` set — `CheckBox` · `Switch` · `RadioButton` · `MenuItemCheckBox` · `MenuItemRadio` — and on no other, `role_from_name` mapping `"switch"` to `Role::Switch`;
 a native `input` whose `type` is exactly `checkbox` or `radio` (the private `is_native_checkable`) reads neither, its native checkedness winning (HTML-AAM), and the builder writes no `toggled` from that native checked state either, so the tree states no native checkbox or radio checked while the snapshot's `checked` reads the element — a measured absence (as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-18-engine-debts/report.md), its fix owned by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line (target: next) — the toggle read per role ratified by the founder (2026-10-18); `aria-invalid`: `true` · `grammar` · `spelling` sets `invalid` `True` · `Grammar` · `Spelling`, an absent, empty (after trimming) or `false` value nothing, and any other value `Invalid::True` (WAI-ARIA 1.2's rule for a value outside the allowed list); the lower-case exact match is a choice — the specification as read states no case rule and no browser was measured — so `TRUE` reads unrecognized: nothing for `aria-selected`, `aria-pressed` and `aria-checked`, invalid for `aria-invalid`; each attribute is read once, and nothing else in the file writes `toggled`; the added lines hold no log site and no panic path — a value of 5,500 characters builds the tree — so what `build_accessibility_tree` returns changes for every document whose markup states one of the four (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:169-213; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:347; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:395-415; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs:134-316 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md); blitz-shell builds the platform tree through the document trait
 — `AccessibilityState::update_tree(&dyn Document)` calls `doc.accessibility_tree()`, from `View::poll` and from `View::build_accessibility_tree` on `InitialTreeRequested`: on a poll that reported work `View::poll` takes the document's changed set (`take_changed_nodes`, outside the `accessibility` cfg, so a shell built without the feature still drains the set and drops it) and, under `accessibility`, calls `update_tree` when the set it took was non-empty — so the platform accessibility adapter receives the tree on change as well as on its initial request, the same crossing and the same content classes (ids as `author_id`, accessible names), more often; since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states the nodes it is handed carry a third content class, states — `selected`, `toggled` and `invalid` on each element node whose markup states them, closed enums and booleans, never an attribute's value as typed — a widening of the adapter crossing ratified by the founder (2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Ратифицировать», the English wording is the overseer's: the builder writes the three states on the node), what an assistive technology reads of them unmeasured until a windowed check — no stand binary builds a platform adapter and the dev host's AT-SPI bus reads inactive — and that witness owned by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line that reads `re-carried:0.2.0`, at an active assistive technology this version does not reach, on the founder's F1 «Пока нет, перенести (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-14), whose headless halves — the tree the shell hands the adapter, read through `&dyn Document`, and the refresh on a Tab and an Enter — are proven on the stand since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:310-352; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:363-410);
 since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync the names class also carries `aria-labelledby`'s computed text, and the nodes carry a fourth content class, descriptions — `aria-description`'s own page text (free, unbounded) and `aria-describedby`'s targets as `described_by` — to the adapter only (the snapshot reads no description), a widening by upstream merge ratified as upstream's behaviour by the founder (2026-10-17, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer, «Утвердить оба (Рекомендую)», both sources confirmed by his «Подтвердить все 10 (Рекомендую)», 2026-10-18), and `aria-expanded` · `aria-disabled` · `aria-level` closed values inside the states class, unmeasured at an assistive technology like the states; what the poll reads, and before 2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff the poll-time refresh did not run (§Document core), so the platform tree was built once; ratified by the founder (2026-10-07) — the shell half of one item with the engine's changed-set contract, "refresh, then drain"; its windowed witness is still owed: no windowed run witnesses the refresh on the dev host — its AT-SPI bus reads inactive and the stand's windowed binary builds blitz-shell without `accessibility` — so it is held by the document-level tests and both feature builds of blitz-shell (packages/blitz-shell/src/accessibility.rs:44-46; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:376-382; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:521-524) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:11; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:110-116; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:56-61); `HtmlDocument` API `from_html`, `query_selector`, `mutate().set_inner_html`, `resolve`, `root_element().final_layout()` (examples/inner_html.rs:12-22; examples/screenshot.rs:103)

- **Events:** `EventHandler::handle_event(node chain, &mut DomEvent, document, EventState)` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:9-17); `NoopEventHandler` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:19-30); `EventDriver::new(doc, handler)` with `handle_ui_event` and `handle_dom_event` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:38-45; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:168; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:310-313; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:35-50), re-exported from the events module (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/mod.rs:9); pointer events produce mouse compatibility events for mouse input and touch events for finger and pen (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:327-349); non-bubbling events reach only the target (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:378-383); focus change dispatches `blur`, `focusout`, `focus`, `focusin` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/focus.rs:15-39); since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction a range input's default actions dispatch `input` — `DomEventData::Input(BlitzInputEvent { value })`, the formatted current value — through the crate-internal `BaseDocument::apply_range_move`, the one write · mark · `Input` · redraw path of its key arms and its pointerdown arm, one per change and none for a move that changes nothing, while its click arm focuses through `generate_focus_events` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:333-354; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:765-777; [Scrolling and input]); since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness `DomEventData::KeyUp` has a default action — `events/mod.rs` routes it to the crate-internal `handle_key_up`, where a released Space on the focused node dispatches `DomEventData::Click` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/mod.rs:12; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/mod.rs:229-230; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:124-144)
 — and `handle_key_or_input_event` dispatches the same Click for a pressed `Enter` on the focused node after its text-input and range arms (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:114-119), both through `dispatch_activation_click`, whose data is `Node::synthetic_click_event_data(modifiers)` and which the event driver queues so the app's handlers (a Dioxus `onclick`) run before the default action `handle_click` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:235-245); `handle_click`'s button arm focuses a `button` or an `input` of type `submit`, `reset` or `button` through `generate_focus_events` before it submits a submit button's form owner (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:909-921; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:984-1001; [Scrolling and input]); `handle_click`, `handle_pointerdown` and `handle_key_or_input_event` keep their signatures — since 2026-10-16-handler-splits-and-readme the bodies of their range and button arms are private named functions, with no behaviour changed for any document: `range_track_fraction` and `press_range_input` for the range pointerdown (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:650-661; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:663-678), `click_button` for the button arm's focus and submit (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:984-1001) and `press_range_input_key` for the range keys (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:146-163), the range ones still writing only through `apply_range_move`, and the range input's private `parse_float` reads its sign, digits and exponent through the private steps `take_sign`, `take_digits` and `take_exponent` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:272-301) — and the Dioxus bridge's converter carries the event's value to `oninput` unchanged; pointer/wheel target the hovered node, keyboard/IME the focused node, falling back to the root (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:217-234);
 `EventState` cancelled / propagation_stopped / redraw_requested with `merge` (packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:13-58); `DomEventKind::from_str` strips `on`, maps `composition` to `Ime` and `change` to `Change` (packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:165-212); `DomEventKind::Change`, after `Input`, and `DomEventData::Change(BlitzInputEvent)` — named `change`, not cancelable, bubbling, with no UI event mapped and no default action — are dispatched by the engine only after `input` on a select's choice, a checkbox, radio or text input firing no engine `change` ([Scrolling and input]) (packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:150; packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:250-251; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/mod.rs:93; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/mod.rs:246-248); per-event `cancelable()`/`bubbles()` tables (packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:366-458); `UiEvent` variants `PointerDown`, `PointerUp`, `PointerMove`, `PointerCancel`, `PointerLeave` (since 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship: `DomEventKind::PointerLeave`, handled by `EventDriver::handle_pointer_leave`, which clears hover — in a hosted sub-document too — and fires the leave events; packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:67-68; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/driver.rs:65-74; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_leave.rs:28-52), `Wheel` with `BlitzWheelDelta::Pixels` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:66-67; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:76-83; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:110); `BlitzPointerId` `Mouse`, `Finger(0)`, `Pen` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:45; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_action.rs:31; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:74); dispatched names include `pointerdown`, `pointermove`, `pointerup`, `pointercancel`, `touchstart`, `touchmove`, `touchend`, `touchcancel`, `mousedown` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:46-62;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:113-120; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:197)

- **Test harness:** blitz-test-harness exports `Harness`, `HarnessOptions`, `key_event`, `mouse_pointer_event`, `pointer_event`, `touch_pointer_event`, `Rect`, `Key`, `Modifiers` and `NamedKey` — re-exports of keyboard-types 0.8's `Key`, `Modifiers` and `NamedKey` (`pub use keyboard_types::{Key, Modifiers, NamedKey};`, `NamedKey` since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync), the types a key press is named with, so a crate that depends on the harness names a key without a dependency of its own — `Busy`, `NotSettled`, `SETTLE_PASS_LIMIT`, `Settled` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/lib.rs:29-34) and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `PixelRect`, `Raster` and `ScreenshotError` from its private module `screenshot` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:10-17; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:19-25; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:27-35); `Harness::screenshot(&mut self) -> Result<Raster, ScreenshotError>` and `Harness::screenshot_rect(&mut self, PixelRect) -> Result<Raster, ScreenshotError>` resolve at the harness's own time (no tick, no pump), paint the viewport at its scale and device size through blitz-paint into `VelloCpuImageRenderer`, then composite the frame over opaque white (premultiplied source-over: each channel `+ (255 - alpha)`, alpha 255); a rectangle is clipped to the viewport and an empty one is `ScreenshotError::EmptyRect`, and a document whose `can_paint_text` reads false is `ScreenshotError::FontsUnavailable` with nothing painted; no path prints, panics or logs; for it the harness depends on three more crates — `blitz-paint` (`default-features = false`, so no `svg` and no `scrollbars` in a per-package build), `anyrender` and `anyrender_vello_cpu` (no `multithreading`) (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:37-103; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md);
